.TH WERKMEISTER-STOP 1 "" "werkmeister" "Werkmeister Manual"
.SH NAME
werkmeister\-stop \- Stop containers without removing them or releasing the slot (use 'infra' for shared infra)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBwerkmeister stop\fR [feature]
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-if\-idle\fR
SessionEnd hook mode: stop the workspace's own feature unless another Claude session is open there; silent, always exits 0, never stops infra
.TP
\fB\-\-idle <minutes>\fR
Stop every workspace's feature containers nothing has used for \e<minutes> (a busy or recently active session, a gate exec or a fresh start all count as use); with [feature], only that one
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Stops a feature's containers without removing them or releasing its slot. Bring it back with \fBwerkmeister restart\fR or \fBwerkmeister up\fR. Use \fBinfra\fR as the feature name to stop the shared infrastructure.
.PP
Two modes run without a person: \fB\-\-if\-idle\fR is the SessionEnd hook behind a workspace's \fBauto_stop\fR, and \fB\-\-idle\fR is one pass of the idle reaper over every workspace.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
werkmeister stop my\-feature
werkmeister stop infra
werkmeister stop \-\-idle 30
.RE
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.PP
\fBwerkmeister down\fR also releases the slot; \fBwerkmeister pause\fR freezes the containers instead.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBwerkmeister\fR(1)
